    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, case-insensitively \u2014 with minimal structural impact.\n\nKey insight: since owner ids increase with creation order, \"owners that existed before this one was created\" is exactly \"owners with a lower id sharing the name.\" That lets the value be derived on demand from the repository, so **no entity or DB-schema changes** were needed.\n\nChanges (4 files, all edits confined to tiny functions):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema, which generates the DTO field/setter.\n2. **`Namesakes.java`** (new, self-contained, WMC_other = 0) \u2014 one static `countBefore(owner, repository)` that counts lower-id owners with a case-insensitive first+last name match.\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** (GET responder, single method) \u2014 sets the field after mapping.\n4. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** (POST responder, single method) \u2014 same, so the create response also carries it.\n\nThe mapper is untouched (MapStruct's default policy just warns on the unmapped target, which is set explicitly in the responders). The new acceptance test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
